id: core/world-field-arena
title: "world, field, and arena"
kind: ontology-contract
status: draft-0.2
updated: 2026-08-13

purpose: >
  Keep the unbounded world, an observer's available information, and the
  provisional slice relevant to action distinct.

definitions:
  reality: >
    Whatever constrains consequences and can disconfirm the current record. It
    is referred to but never serialized as though the model exhausts it.
  world_horizon: >
    The open-ended environment exceeding every present agent, arena, and map.
  field: >
    Signals available to an attributed observer through sources, memory,
    perception, tools, relationships, body, and environment at a time.
  arena: >
    A provisional agent-relative relevance boundary: purpose, participants,
    affordances, impediments, resources, constraints, authority, stakes,
    horizon, inclusions, exclusions, and open lacunae.
  agent_space: >
    An ownership, security, and event-stream namespace. It is not an arena.

relation: "world horizon -> attributed field -> provisional arena"

arena_minimum:
  - purpose-or-question
  - participant-and-affected-agent-refs
  - affordances-and-impediments
  - constraints-and-resources
  - authority-privacy-and-egress-boundaries
  - inclusion-and-exclusion-rules
  - open-lacunae-and-frame-limits
  - source-refs-and-as-of-time

invariants:
  - "World is not an alias for arena."
  - "Arena is not an alias for Yawn."
  - "An arena remains provisional and may be reframed."
  - "A field is observer-relative and incomplete."
  - "The model keeps excluded context and unknowns visible when consequential."
  - "A software agent may be represented operationally without claiming human-like experience."

counterexamples:
  - "A world UI whose visible objects are treated as all of reality."
  - "A folder called Work treated as one arena without participants or boundary."
  - "A vector search result silently accepted as arena membership."

links:
  - spec/ontology.md
  - spec/routing.md
  - shape/information-field.yawn
  - core/holarchy.yawn
  - core/turn.yawn
